  "description": "Octopus is tough in more ways than one. Sure, it's literally tough and requires some technique to make it palatable, but it's also tough in that it has no problem standing up to strongly flavored ingredients. Like kimchi. Octopus is great with kimchi.",
  "notes": "Notes: Boiled octopus can be found in most Japanese markets. If making from scratch, boil a large pot of salted water. Add octopus to the pot and cook until it's just cooked through to the center, about 10 minutes. Shock in ice water and chill thoroughly before slicing. Gochugaru (Korean chile flakes) can be found in any Korean grocery and most other Asian groceries.",
